<h2 style="clear: both; font-family: 'Tahoma', sans-serf; font-size: 18pt;">&nbsp;</h2>
<h2 style="clear: both; font-family: 'Tahoma', sans-serf; font-size: 18pt;">Resources</h2>
<hr />
<p>LTCC offers the same support services to all students, whether you are taking classes face to face, online, or both.</p>
<p>Information on all LTCC support services can be found on the <a title="Campus Resources" href="https://www.ltcc.edu/campusresources/index.php">Campus Resources </a>page. Below are a few that may be particularly helpful for online students.</p>
<ul>
<li><a title="Counseling Services " href="https://www.ltcc.edu/campusresources/counseling.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Counseling Services </a></li>
<li><a title="Disability Resource Center" href="https://www.ltcc.edu/campusresources/studentaccessibilityservices/index.php">Disability Resource Center</a></li>
<li><a title="Financial Aid" href="https://www.ltcc.edu/admissions/financial-aid/index.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Financial Aid</a></li>
<li><a title="Forms" href="https://www.ltcc.edu/admissions/forms.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Forms</a></li>
<li><a title="Library" href="https://www.ltcc.edu/campusresources/library/index.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Library </a></li>
<li><a title="Scholarships" href="https://www.ltcc.edu/giving/donate/scholarships.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Scholarships</a></li>
<li><a title="Tutoring and Learning Center" href="https://www.ltcc.edu/campusresources/tutoring_center.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Tutoring and Learning Center</a></li>
</ul>
<p>LTCC is primarily operating in a remote capacity during the COVID pandemic. Most of our services and classes are being held online. A great deal of information about how to navigate LTCC during these times can be found on <a href="http://ltcc.edu/academics/virtual_campus/index.php">our Virtual Campus webpages</a>.</p>
<h2 style="clear: both; font-family: 'Tahoma', sans-serf; font-size: 18pt;">&nbsp;</h2>
<h2 style="clear: both; font-family: 'Tahoma', sans-serf; font-size: 18pt;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<hr />
<h6 class="snippet-spacer"><b>DO NOT EDIT THIS TEXT (content in this row will not appear on page).</b> <br />Enter the heading in the left cell, and the body that displays when you expand the row in the right cell. To add another row to the accordian, add another row to the table.</h6>
<table class="ou_accordion">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Accordian ID (must be unique if more than one accordian on page)</td>
<td>accordion1</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Do you have online classes?</span></td>
<td>Yes, we do! We offer Hybrid, EVE, and DE courses - all of these are described more fully below.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Can anyone take an online course?</span></td>
<td>All online courses are open to students who meet the regular course requirements. It is strongly recommended that you take the <a href="https://www.sbctc.edu/becoming-a-student/right-degree-you/is-online-learning-for-me.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Is Online Learning For Me?</a> quiz to determine if an online course is right for you. EVE courses at LTCC are online, but feel more like face-to-face. DE classes are also online, but they are more like traditional online courses that require students to be more organized and self-reliant. Read more about the different kinds of online courses LTCC offers below.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><span style="font-size: 12pt;">What if I live in a state outside of California?<br /></span></td>
<td>Due in part to the increased popularity of distance education, many states have prescribed an &ldquo;authorization&rdquo; process for out-of-state institutions delivering online programs to its state residents. States are attempting through these processes to ensure quality post-secondary education, to preserve the integrity of an academic degree and to instill greater consumer protection for their student citizens. Please read LTCC's policy on <a title="State Authorization of Distance Education Outside of California" href="{{f:48331110}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">State Authorization of Distance Education Outside of California</a> to see if your state is on LTCC's list of approved states.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><span style="font-size: 12pt;">What is a Hybrid Course?</span></td>
<td>
<p>A Hybrid course is a course with both face-to-face and online components. At LTCC, these often include classes with hands-on training requirements that lead to particular credentials and licenses, along with some science labs. <a href="https://www.ltcc.edu/academics/hybrid.php">Read more about Hybrid courses</a> at LTCC.</p>
<p>Hear more about each <a href="https://youtu.be/xyHAa3GK6Wk">course modality &rarr;&nbsp;&nbsp;</a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><span style="font-size: 12pt;">What is an EVE Course?<br /></span></td>
<td>
<p>EVE, or Enhanced Virtual Education, are courses that are delivered online but that provide a lot of the interaction and support you'd find in a face-to-face class. LTCC's EVE classes offer great support, more discussion and interaction with other students and faculty, and offer some synchronous work activities. <a href="https://www.ltcc.edu/academics/eve.php">Read more about EVE classes</a> at LTCC.</p>
<p>Hear more about each <a href="https://youtu.be/xyHAa3GK6Wk">course modality &rarr; &nbsp;</a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><span style="font-size: 12pt;">What is a DE Course? <br /></span></td>
<td>
<p>DE, or Distance Education, are traditional online courses that require students to be organized and self-driven to succeed. These courses are very flexible and convenient for busy students, allowing for students to often set their own pace. <a href="https://www.ltcc.edu/academics/de.php">Read more about DE classes</a> at LTCC.</p>
<p>Hear more about each <a href="https://youtu.be/xyHAa3GK6Wk">course modality &rarr; &nbsp;</a></p>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></ouc:div>
  	
